SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: Understanding Brain Health
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confi
 rmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186163\n\n5:00PM 
 Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nWhat if brain health wasn’t just clinical
 —but personal\, preventative\, and deeply relevant to how we live every 
 day? In honor of Alzheimer's Awareness Month\, this candid\, forward-think
 ing conversation brings together leading physicians and patient voices to 
 explore the latest in neurovascular innovation\, life-saving interventions
 \, and the often-overlooked habits that shape cognitive well-being. Expect
  an unfiltered look at survival\, prevention\, and the science redefining 
 how we think about the brain.\n\nFeaturing Dr. Christopher Ogilvy—Direct
 or of Endovascular and Operative Neurovascular Surgery at Beth Israel Deac
 oness Medical Center and Professor at Harvard Medical School—whose pione
 ering work continues to push the boundaries of modern neurosurgery\, alon
 gside Meg Smith\, CEO of Cure Alzheimer’s Fund. Since taking the helm in
  2023\, Smith has led the organization’s continued growth and impact\, a
 dvancing a research model that has directed over $138 million toward bold 
 scientific efforts to slow\, prevent\, and ultimately reverse Alzheimer’
 s.\n\nTogether with additional expert and patient perspectives\, the panel
  offers a rare opportunity to engage with leaders at the forefront of brai
 n health and discovery.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for m
 embers only. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/186163
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-187622@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260610T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260610T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Checkmate" with Ben Mezrich
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 13 spots left\nS
 tatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/even
 ts/187622\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion \nStep into the high-st
 akes world of Checkmate with bestselling author Ben Mezrich—an electrify
 ing true story that unravels the biggest scandal in modern chess.\n\nIn Se
 ptember 2022\, the chess world was shaken when nineteen-year-old American 
 prodigy Hans Niemann defeated reigning world champion Magnus Carlsen in a 
 stunning upset. Days later\, Carlsen accused Niemann of cheating—an alle
 gation that ignited a global firestorm\, drawing in Chess.com\, the media\
 , and a rapidly expanding digital audience. What followed was a dramatic c
 ollision of reputation\, rivalry\, and power.\n\nBut Checkmate is about fa
 r more than controversy. It’s a portrait of ambition at its sharpest edg
 e—a young player willing to risk everything to rise\, and a legendary fi
 gure determined to defend his legacy. Set against the backdrop of a centur
 ies-old game transformed by streaming\, sponsorships\, and Silicon Valley 
 influence\, Mezrich brings readers inside a world that is as cutthroat as 
 it is cerebral.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members o
 nly. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/187622
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
